peedup\": 1.9287341591885712, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 1.9320091477744028}, \"decision\": \"accept\", \"decision_reason\": \"Correct on all 5 workloads; geomean 1.929x >> 1.0. Confirms H1 (native fp32 atomics beat torch bf16 CAS even with +~300MB init/finalize passes). Largest gains on BW/L2-bound W2/W3 (~2.05x), smallest on launch-bound W1 (1.73x). Becomes best-so-far / parent for next candidate.\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 1, \"skill_usage\": {\"KernelWiki\": \"not-used (A800 sm_80 Ampere; KernelWiki covers Hopper/Blackwell only, out of scope)\"}, \"notes\": \"W1 (1.73x) lags others, consistent with launch-overhead + fp32-scratch pass tax on the small L2-resident workload -> motivates c002 (B1 memset+fused finalize, fewer bytes) and later a bf16-direct probe (c003) for the L2-resident regime. Correctness margin comfortable (99% matched-ratio gate met; max_abs 0.25 on <=1% tail expected from bf16 rounding vs non-deterministic reference).\"}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
